---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | 3DPrintingCostCalc.com"
  description="Privacy policy for 3DPrintingCostCalc.com. All 3D files (.stl, .3mf, .gcode) are parsed 100% locally in your browser with zero server uploads."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', item: 'https://3dprintingcostcalc.com/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', item: 'https://3dprintingcostcalc.com/privacy/' }
  ]}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">Last Updated: October 2026</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Highlight Box -->
    <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-cyan-950/40 border border-cyan-500/30 text-xs sm:text-sm text-cyan-200 leading-relaxed">
      <strong>Core Privacy Guarantee:</strong> 3DPrintingCostCalc.com is an entirely stateless client-side web utility. When you drop, upload, or select a 3D model file (.stl, .3mf, .gcode, .bgcode, or .obj), the file is read, triangulated, and parsed entirely inside your local browser memory using modern JavaScript Web APIs. <strong>No 3D models, CAD geometries, intellectual property, or G-code toolpaths are ever uploaded or transmitted to our servers or any third party.</strong>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. Zero-Upload Architecture -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">1. Zero-Server File Inspection Architecture</h2>
      <p>
        Traditional online quoting tools require users to upload confidential CAD models to remote cloud servers for geometry rendering and volume calculations. 3DPrintingCostCalc.com operates on a strict zero-upload model:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
        <li><strong>Binary STL & OBJ:</strong> Facets, normal vectors, and signed vertex volumes are computed client-side using JavaScript typed arrays (<code class="text-cyan-400 font-mono">ArrayBuffer</code> / <code class="text-cyan-400 font-mono">DataView</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>3MF Packages:</strong> XML metadata, slicer configs, and ZIP container archives are extracted in browser memory.</li>
        <li><strong>G-code & BGCODE:</strong> Slicer header comments, extrusion volume markers, toolhead speeds, and acceleration commands are parsed line-by-line via local Web Streams.</li>
        <li><strong>Volatile Memory:</strong> Once you reload or close your browser tab, all parsed mesh coordinates and file buffers are immediately purged from your system's RAM.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Information We Do Not Collect -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">2. Personal Data We Do Not Collect</h2>
      <p>
        Because our service requires no user account creation, registration, or sign-in, we do not request, harvest, or store:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
        <li>Personal identifying information (names, email addresses, phone numbers, or physical mailing addresses).</li>
        <li>Credit card details, bank information, or billing data (all calculators and tools on this website are 100% free to use).</li>
        <li>Proprietary 3D design files, industrial blueprints, or customer quote databases.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Local Storage & Client-Side Configuration -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">3. Local Storage & Device Preferences</h2>
      <p>
        To deliver a seamless user experience, our application uses standard HTML5 <code class="text-cyan-400 font-mono">localStorage</code> on your local device to remember:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
        <li>Your selected color theme preference (Light Mode vs. Dark Mode).</li>
        <li>Your default machine profile selection and local electricity utility rate ($/kWh).</li>
        <li>Your custom hourly labor rate and commercial markup percentages.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information never leaves your browser and is never synchronized to an external cloud database. You can clear or reset this data at any time by clearing your browser cache and local website cookies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Shareable URL Parameters -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">4. Shareable URL Parameters</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the "Share Quote URL" feature, current calculator inputs (such as spool cost, print duration, part weight, and printer model) are serialized directly into the URL query string (<code class="text-cyan-400 font-mono">?printer=...&amp;weight=...</code>). This state is held entirely within the URL link itself and is not logged, registered, or cataloged on any database server.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. Cookies & Web Analytics -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">5. Cookies & Privacy-Preserving Web Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We may use aggregate web analytics (such as Cloudflare Web Analytics or Google Analytics 4) to monitor general site reliability, server uptime, geographic distribution, and device browser types. Cloudflare Web Analytics operates without stateful client tracking cookies and does not follow users across third-party websites or construct advertising profiles.
      </p>
      <p>
        If Google Analytics is active, IP anonymization is enforced to prevent individual visitor identification.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 6. Third-Party Advertising & Cookies -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">6. Third-Party Advertising Partners & Opt-Out</h2>
      <p>
        To keep 3DPrintingCostCalc.com free for the maker and manufacturing community, we may display third-party advertisements (such as Google AdSense). These third-party vendors and ad networks may use cookies and web beacons to serve ads based on prior visits to our website or other sites on the web.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-slate-300">
        <li>Google Ads Settings: <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-400 underline hover:text-cyan-300">https://adssettings.google.com</a></li>
        <li>Network Advertising Initiative Opt-Out: <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-400 underline hover:text-cyan-300">https://optout.networkadvertising.org</a></li>
        <li>Digital Advertising Alliance Consumer Choice: <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-400 underline hover:text-cyan-300">https://www.aboutads.info/choices</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 7. Affiliate Links & External Tools -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">7. Affiliate Links & Hardware Vendor Disclosures</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages on this site may contain affiliate referral links to 3D printer manufacturers, filament distributors (e.g., Bambu Lab, Polymaker, Sunlu, eSUN, Creality), or Amazon Associates. Clicking these links may result in a small commission for this website at zero extra cost to you. We only recommend hardware and materials vetted by active 3D printing practitioners.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 8. GDPR & CCPA/CPRA Compliance -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">8. Your Rights Under GDPR & CCPA/CPRA</h2>
      <p>
        Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and California Consumer Privacy Act / California Privacy Rights Act (CCPA/CPRA), users are entitled to specific rights regarding their personal data:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
        <li><strong>Right to Know & Access:</strong> Because we do not collect personal records, accounts, or file uploads, we hold no personal data profile on your identity.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Deletion:</strong> All user-configurable values reside in your device's browser memory and can be erased instantly by clearing your browser's site data.</li>
        <li><strong>Do Not Sell My Personal Information:</strong> We do not sell, rent, or trade user data or CAD files to third parties.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 9. Children's Privacy -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">9. Children's Online Privacy Protection (COPPA)</h2>
      <p>
        3DPrintingCostCalc.com is intended for general audiences, STEM educators, students, and professional makers. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 10. Data Security & HTTPS -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">10. Data Security & TLS Encryption</h2>
      <p>
        All communications between your browser and 3DPrintingCostCalc.com are encrypted using modern Transport Layer Security (TLS 1.3 / HTTPS). Because all calculations occur locally, your 3D files are protected from network interception and man-in-the-middle data snooping.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 11. Policy Changes & Updates -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">11. Revisions to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect enhancements in web technology, browser security capabilities, or regulatory requirements. Any modifications will be posted directly to this page with an updated effective date.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 12. Contact Information -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">12. Contact Information & Inquiries</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions, feedback, or concerns regarding our privacy guarantees or client-side calculation architecture, please reach out to us at:
      </p>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0e1628] border border-white/10 font-mono text-xs">
        <p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@3dprintingcostcalc.com" class="text-cyan-400 underline hover:text-cyan-300">support@3dprintingcostcalc.com</a></p>
        <p class="text-slate-400 mt-1">Website: <a href="https://3dprintingcostcalc.com" class="text-cyan-400 underline hover:text-cyan-300">https://3dprintingcostcalc.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
